---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for NanophotonicsLab — how data is handled across simulation tools and the Methods Assistant.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container privacy-content">

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Simulation tools</h2>
        <p>
          All numerical simulation tools (Mie, BEM, RCWA, BPM, plasmonic nanoparticles,
          cylinder dispersion, photothermal, and all calculators) run <strong>entirely
          in your browser</strong>. No input data, parameters or results are sent to
          any server. Your data never leaves your device.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tools that use <a href="https://pyodide.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyodide</a>
          (BEM Solver, RCWA) download Python packages on first use (~35 MB). These
          packages are fetched from public CDNs and cached locally by your browser.
          No user data is included in these requests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Methods Assistant</h2>
        <p>
          The Methods Assistant has two modes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Semantic search</strong> (default): runs locally in your browser
            using an embedded language model. No data leaves your device.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI synthesis</strong> (optional): requires an Anthropic API key
            provided by you. When enabled, your query and the retrieved context are
            sent directly to <code>api.anthropic.com</code>. NanophotonicsLab does
            not operate any backend or proxy — the request goes straight from your
            browser to Anthropic's API.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>API key handling</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The key is stored in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> only if you choose to save it.</li>
          <li>It is never sent anywhere other than <code>api.anthropic.com</code>.</li>
          <li>You can delete it at any time using the "Clear key" button in the Assistant, or by clearing your browser's site data.</li>
          <li><strong>Recommendation:</strong> use a restricted or non-production API key. Do not use keys with billing access beyond what you're comfortable with.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          NanophotonicsLab uses <a href="https://umami.is" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami</a>
          for anonymous, aggregated usage analytics. Umami is privacy-friendly:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>No cookies</li>
          <li>No personal data collected</li>
          <li>No cross-site tracking</li>
          <li>GDPR compliant</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Analytics data includes page views, referrer, browser type and country
          (derived from IP, which is not stored). No individual user profiles are created.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          NanophotonicsLab does not use cookies. The following data may be stored
          in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> (light/dark) — stored as <code>theme</code></li>
          <li><strong>Anthropic API key</strong> (Methods Assistant only, if you choose to save it) — stored as <code>anthropic-api-key</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can clear all stored data at any time through your browser settings
          or by using the controls provided in the relevant tool.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — the Inter typeface is loaded from <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code>. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Anthropic API</strong> — only when you explicitly use AI synthesis in the Methods Assistant. See <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Pyodide CDN</strong> — Python WebAssembly packages loaded on demand for BEM and RCWA tools.</li>
          <li><strong>Umami Cloud</strong> — anonymous analytics. See <a href="https://umami.is/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy-block">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy or data handling:
          <a href="mailto:info@nanophotonicslab.com">info@nanophotonicslab.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: calc(var(--space-3xl) + var(--space-lg)) 0 var(--space-xl);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .privacy-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .privacy-block h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .privacy-block p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-block p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .privacy-block ul {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-block li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .privacy-block a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .privacy-block a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .privacy-block code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 4px);
  }
</style>
